  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "update_errors_warnings",
    "file": "php-src/ext/date/php_date.c",
    "description": "`update_errors_warnings()` stores `*last_errors` into the global `DATEG(last_errors)` when warnings/errors exist, but then unconditionally calls `timelib_error_container_dtor(*last_errors)` and nulls only the local pointer. This leaves `DATEG(last_errors)` dangling (UAF). Later, request/module shutdown (`zm_post_zend_deactivate_date`) calls `timelib_error_container_dtor(DATEG(last_errors))` again, causing use-after-free/double-dtor access in `timelib_error_container_dtor`.",
    "conditions": "Trigger any DateTime parse path that produces at least one warning/error so `(*last_errors)->warning_count || error_count` is true (e.g., PoC `<?new DateTime('\\xff');`). Data flow: fuzz input executes PHP code -> `DateTime::__construct` -> `php_date_initialize` -> `timelib_strtotime(...,&err,...)` allocates error container -> `update_errors_warnings(&err)` assigns global then frees same container -> at post-deactivate shutdown, global `DATEG(last_errors)` is destroyed again, producing heap-use-after-free."
  },
